# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# THIS FILE IS INERT ON GITHUB PAGES, the current production origin. Pages serves
# every asset with `Cache-Control: max-age=600` and gives no way to change it, so the
# lifetime visitors actually get today is whatever the Cloudflare zone's Browser
# Cache TTL overrides it to — measured 2026-08-04: 4h on openmaptiles.org, 8h on the
# labs.maptiler.com staging host. Both numbers live in the Cloudflare dashboard
# (Caching -> Configuration), not in this repo. Editing this file changes nothing
# until the site moves to Cloudflare Pages; see DEPLOYMENT.md.
#
# It exists for the same reason `_redirects` does: so that move needs no second pass.
# Jekyll skips underscore-prefixed files, so `_config.yml` names it under `include:`,
# and script/verify-build asserts it reaches _site/ and that every directory it
# mentions still exists — this is otherwise the kind of file that rots silently,
# since nothing about the live site changes when it is wrong.
#
# 30 days, not the year Lighthouse asks for. Filenames here are not content-hashed
# (`img/header-map-2560px.png`, `img/styles/openmaptiles.webp`), so the TTL is also
# how long a repeat visitor keeps a stale copy after the file is replaced, and an
# edge purge does not reach a browser already holding one. 30d clears Lighthouse's
# threshold; a year would trade a passing audit for imagery no deploy can correct.
# Fingerprint the filenames first if you want `immutable`.
#
# /assets/ gets 1 day for that same reason, and deliberately not 30. core.css and
# main.js are unhashed too, but a stale stylesheet or module is a broken layout or a
# dead interaction rather than an out-of-date photo, and it is the copy every page
# depends on. A day is short enough that a fix lands on its own; raising it means
# accepting that a CSS or JS regression stays live for repeat visitors for that long.
#
# Only directories that hold nothing but static assets are listed. /styles/ is NOT
# one of them despite the name: the style thumbnails live under /img/styles/, while
# /styles/:slug/ are the generated HTML pages from _plugins/datapage_generator.rb
# and have to stay short-lived. HTML is left unlisted throughout for that reason.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400

/img/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/media/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/favicon.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000

/favicon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=2592000
